{
  "explanation": "An attacker leveraged a compromised www-data web server user account to exploit misconfigured sudo privileges, allowing them to append an SSH public key to the root user's authorized_keys file. This action establishes unauthorized long-term remote access and persistence on the target system. The status indicates that the command successfully executed, granting the attacker root-level access via SSH.",
  "mitre_tactic": "Persistence",
  "recommended_actions": [
    "Immediately review and clean the /root/.ssh/authorized_keys file to remove any unauthorized public keys.",
    "Revoke the sudo privileges of the www-data user in the /etc/sudoers configuration to prevent arbitrary root command execution from the web application.",
    "Conduct a thorough forensic investigation of the web-01 host to identify the initial vector of compromise within the web application."
  ]
}
